Title: "Axiom"
Id: "1f2a0a6b-a9b9-4d81-b636-5e0c10d6fbdb"

Text: "`Axiom:` is a theorem-like top-level item.

```mlg-fragment
[\\command]?
Axiom:
given?: <RefinedDeclarationStatement>+
where?: <ClauseUnion>+
then: <ClauseUnion>+
iff?: <ClauseUnion>+
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
Aliases?: <AliasItemUnion>+
Writing?: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Metadata?: <MetadataItemUnion>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

The optional heading is a `[\\command]` command header. The `Axiom:` section
takes **no** argument; the result's name goes in `Documented:` `called:`.

```mlg-fragment
[\\empty.set.axiom]
Axiom:
then: exists: X where: X is \\set
Documented:
. called: \"Axiom of the Empty Set\"
Id: \"23e4567e-e89b-42d3-a456-426614174000\"
```

The `then:` section is required. `given:` accepts refined-capable declaration
statements.

The checker validates syntax, references, symbols, and requirements. It does not
prove that theorem-like conclusions follow mathematically from their
assumptions."
Id: "e232d3c6-7519-4fc8-a696-ec496d1bde61"
